  "result": "The two decisions sit in two places.\n\n- **At sign-in:** `src/server/services/session-service.ts` sets `SESSION_TTL_DAYS = 30`. Creating a session computes `expiresAt` as now plus 30 days.\n- **On a later request:** `src/lib/session.ts` compares `expiresAt` to `Date.now()` and returns `null` once it has passed. The same check also appears in `src/server/repositories/session-repository.ts`, where the lookup returns `null` for a row with `expiresAt <= now`. That repository check is what actually rejects an expired session, so I've included it.\n\nANSWER: src/server/services/session-service.ts, src/lib/session.ts, src/server/repositories/session-repository.ts",
